cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRI-27 ISA findings, please cite this work. Balanced ternary instruction set with 27 registers in Coptic 3-bank encoding."
title: "Trinity B003: TRI-27 ISA — Balanced Ternary Instruction Set Architecture"
abstract: "We present TRI-27, a balanced ternary instruction set architecture with 36 opcodes and 27 registers organized in Coptic 3-bank encoding. Key innovations include: (1) TRI-27 ISA specification with 36 opcodes (arithmetic, memory, branch, I/O, special); (2) Coptic alphabet encoding with 3 banks (Alpha: α-η, Iota: ι-ρ, Sigma: σ-ϡ) of 9 registers each; (3) 3-bank validation preventing cross-bank register operations; (4) T27 binary format for episode encoding with trit-level compression. The architecture enables 3^21 unique states from 27 registers while maintaining hardware simplicity. Register file uses balanced ternary representation {-1, 0, +1} with Trit27 encoding (2 bits/trit). Pure Zig implementation with emulator, assembler, and binary encoder. Complete ISA reference with cycle counts, encoding tables, and example programs."
